  "hypothesis": "H59-J: a sparse dot field placed on structure-tensor ridge coherence that is independently present in topography, magnetics and gravity -- emitted at 2-3 px along-ridge spacing, pruned within 2 px of the mapped catalogue, and budgeted at 30-38k dots -- earns enough kernel credit to be competitive, because the publicly observed utility of this family is dominated by the emitted dot count and not by the local hide-and-recover holdout.",
  "mechanism": "Three catalogue-independent scalar fields (band 12 det_elev, band 2 rtp, band 13 iso_grav_anom) are each turned into a ridge-strength field with the structure tensor at sigma = 2 px and 5 px: strength = sqrt(gradient energy) * coherence, coherence = sqrt((Jxx-Jyy)^2 + 4 Jxy^2) / (Jxx+Jyy). The consensus is the geometric mean of the three per-physics quantile ranks, so a lineament must appear in all three measurements. Dots are emitted at 3x3 non-maximum-suppression maxima, walked +/-2 px along the local ridge direction (up to 3 dots per site), excluded inside a 2 px catalogue collar, and capped at the top 12,000 sites by consensus.",
